      "reasoning": "Article 54(5) allows derogation only within territory under a party’s own control and only when required by imperative military necessity. Here the wells and stores were destroyed while Drennick was withdrawing from Calvaran territory, not within territory it controlled. Moreover, the destruction was not essential to any immediate military operation; Drennick already possessed its own water and food supplies. The resulting lack of water and food for 6,000 civilians demonstrates that the act would cause starvation, which the treaty expressly forbids even in cases of necessity.",
